-- title:
--   Abel–Jacobi commutes with reduction onto the étale component
-- statement:
--   The setting is the two-chart integral model of the modular curve $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring and its special fibre, described by the following data.
--
--   Arithmetic data: a prime $p$; an integer $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$; an intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq L((t))$ equal (hypothesis `hK`) to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$; a discrete valuation ring $A$ which is a domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAp`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that of $L$; and an element $j \in K$ whose image in $L((t))$ is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (`hj`), assumed nonzero. The scheme $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) with its structural morphism $\pi =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ is assumed proper.
--
--   Special-fibre data: an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$ that is an $A$-algebra; two proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$, geometrically integral curves $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$; closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ of $C_1, C_2$ into the base change $X_k$ (the pullback of $\pi$ along $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$) over $k$; the hypothesis `hcover` that every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; and `hred`, `hn`, `hn0`, asserting that the intersection $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ is reduced with cardinality $n > 0$.
--
--   Sections and Picard data: a section $\varepsilon$ of $\pi$, sections $\varepsilon_1$ of $c_1$ and $\varepsilon_2$ of $c_2$, and `hε₁` saying that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ is the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $k$. A relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation $D$ for $\pi$ (a scheme $D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ with a zero section), together with `hrep`: $D$ represents, via `algEquivZeroCut`, the subfunctor of rigidified line bundles on $X$ that are fibrewise algebraically equivalent to zero; $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is assumed smooth (`hsm`) and separated (`hsep`). Likewise `hreps` represents that subfunctor for $X_k$ by the base change $D_k$, and `hPk` asserts that its Poincaré bundle is isomorphic to the base change along $k$ of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep.some`. Designations $D_1$ for $c_1$ and $D_2$ for $c_2$ with representability hypotheses `hrep₁`, `hrep₂`.
--
--   Comparison of Jacobians: a morphism $\nu_2$ from $D_k.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $k$, with `hν₂` expressing, for every $k$-scheme $T$ and every $T$-point $a$ of $D_k$, that the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₂.some` along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ is isomorphic to the `rigidify`-normalisation (relative to the rigidifying section of $\varepsilon_2$ and the projection $\mathrm{pr}_2$) of the pullback along `curveChange i₂.1` of the bundle obtained from `hreps.poincare` by pulling back along $a$.
--
--   Generic fibre data: algebra structures making $A \to L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ a tower; a curve model $M_\eta$ (in the sense of `CurveModel`: an integral, proper, smooth relative dimension one scheme with a ring isomorphism of the given field onto its function field, compatible with the base field, and a bijection from closed points to places) over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182), with an isomorphism $e_\eta$ from $M_\eta.C$ onto the base change of $X$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`heη`).
--
--   Group-theoretic bookkeeping of the special fibre: a structure $G$ of type [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9), consisting of abelian groups $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$, a subgroup $G.\mathrm{torus} \le G.J0s$ and a surjective homomorphism $G.\mathrm{proj} : G.J0s \to G.JI \times G.JE$ with kernel $G.\mathrm{torus}$; bijections `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` identifying $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$ with the $k$-points of $D_k.\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_1.\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ respectively; hypotheses `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` that each of these bijections turns addition into tensor product of the corresponding pulled-back Poincaré bundles; and `hproj` that for each $x \in G.J0s$ the first component of $G.\mathrm{proj}\, x$ corresponds under `ptsI` to `pts x` followed by the comparison morphism `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom i₁.1 i₁.2 hε₁ hreps hrep₁.some`, and the second component corresponds under `ptsE` to `pts x` followed by $\nu_2$.
--
--   Generic Abel–Jacobi data: a bijection `gpts` from $\mathrm{JOne}(Mp) = \mathrm{Pic}^0(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}, \overline{\mathbb{Q}}(X_1(Mp)))$ onto the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$, additive for the relative group law of `hrep.some` (`hgadd`). Further, a representability statement `hDL` over $L$, an $X_L$-point $\mathrm{ajL}$ of $D_L$, a morphism $kL$ between the base changes of $X$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and to $L$, a morphism $\mathrm{ajbar}$ from $M_\eta.C$ to $D.P$, a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\bar\varepsilon$ of $M_\eta.C$, and the hypotheses `hPL` (the Poincaré bundle over $L$ is the base change of that over $A$), `hajLε` ($\mathrm{ajL}$ sends the section $\varepsilon_L$ to the zero section), `hajL` (for every field $K'$ and every $K'$-point $x$ of $X_L$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle along $x$ followed by $\mathrm{ajL}$ is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor cut out by $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor cut out by $\varepsilon_L$), `hkL₁`, `hkL₂` (compatibility of $kL$ with the two projections), `hajbar` (the formula $\mathrm{ajbar} = e_\eta$ followed by $kL$, $\mathrm{ajL}$ and $\mathrm{pr}_1$), `hajbar_over`, `hεbar`, `hεbar_aj` (that $\bar\varepsilon$ lies over $\varepsilon$ and is sent to the zero section), and `hpts_aj`: for any two $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ lying over $\varepsilon$, there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ on `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` equal to $[x] - [s]$ under the place correspondence $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ whose class satisfies $\mathrm{gpts}(\mathrm{Pic}^0\text{-class of } D_v) = x$ followed by $\mathrm{ajbar}$.
--
--   Igusa-side data on the component $C_2$: an integral weight one form $w$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $k$ (a modular form with an integral $q$-expansion whose reduction is nonzero), the associated Igusa function field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35), a curve model $\mathrm{Mdl}_2$ of it over $k$ with an isomorphism $e_2 : \mathrm{Mdl}_2.C \cong C_2$ over $k$ (`he₂`); an additive bijection $\theta_2$ from $G.JE$ onto $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the Igusa field, pinned by `hθpin₂`: whenever $g \in G.JE$ and a $k$-point $x$ of $C_2$ are such that the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₂.some` along `ptsE g` is isomorphic to the line bundle of the divisor cut by $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor cut by $\varepsilon_2$, there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ equal to $[x] - [\varepsilon_2]$ (places taken through $\mathrm{Mdl}_2.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ after transport by $e_2^{-1}$) with $\theta_2 g$ its class.
--
--   Reduction data: a valuation subring $\mathrm{Pl}$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ in its nonunits (`hPl`), a ring homomorphism $\rho : A \to \mathrm{Pl}$ compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hρ`), a subring $O \le \mathrm{Pl}$ with $\rho_O : A \to O$ likewise compatible (`hρO`), and a surjective homomorphism $\pi_k : \mathrm{Pl} \to k$ with $A \to k$ equal to $\pi_k \circ \rho$ (`hAlgk`, `hπk`). Finally a map $\mathrm{red}_2$ from places of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to places of the Igusa field over $k$, pinned by `hred₂`: for a place $P$, an $O$-point $\xi$ of $X$ and a $k$-point $c$ of $C_2$, if $\xi$ restricted along $O \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $X$ corresponding to $P$ (through $M_\eta.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}^{-1}$ and $e_\eta$), and $c$ followed by $i_2$ and $\mathrm{pr}_1$ is $\xi$ composed with the reduction $\pi_k \circ (O \hookrightarrow \mathrm{Pl})$, then $\mathrm{red}_2 P$ is the place of $\mathrm{Mdl}_2$ attached to the point $c$ transported by $e_2^{-1}$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is: for every degree-zero divisor $D_v$ on [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that every place $P$ in the support of $D_v$ admits an $O$-point $\xi$ of $X$ and a $k$-point $c$ of $C_2$ with (i) $\xi$ restricted to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equal to the point of $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ attached to $P$, (ii) $c$ followed by $i_2$ and $\mathrm{pr}_1$ equal to $\xi$ composed with the reduction map, and (iii) no point of $c$'s image lying in the image of the second projection of $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ — that is, the reduction avoids the intersection points of the two components — and for every $O$-point $z$ of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ such that $\mathrm{gpts}$ of the class of $D_v$ equals $z$ restricted along $O \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and for every $y \in G.J0s$ whose associated $k$-point of $D_k$, followed by the first projection, equals $z$ composed with the reduction $\pi_k \circ (O \hookrightarrow \mathrm{Pl})$, and for every degree-zero divisor $\bar D$ on the Igusa function field whose underlying divisor is the pushforward `Finsupp.mapDomain red₂` of $D_v$, one has
--   $$\theta_2\bigl((G.\mathrm{proj}\, y)_2\bigr) = \text{the class of } \bar D \text{ in } \mathrm{Pic}^0(k, \text{Igusa field}).$$
--
--   This is the compatibility of the Abel–Jacobi map with reduction on the étale component $C_2$ of the special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$: the class of a degree-zero divisor whose support reduces into $C_2$ away from the intersection with $C_1$ has, as its image under the $C_2$-component of the projection from the special fibre group $G.J0s$, exactly the class of the reduced divisor on the Igusa curve. It is the input used in the identification of Hecke and diamond operators on the $C_2$-part of the special fibre in the Eichler–Shimura style statements that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_addEquiv_proj_snd_eq_pic0Mk_mapDomain_of_points_eq_reduction_of_surjective_residue_of_forall_mem_support_exists_section_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

